From 5ec6e371f62721c8ba3b098748b836ce613a525a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taimoor Ul Islam <tislam@iastate.edu>
Date: Sat, 27 Jun 2026 17:53:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 09/53] kaiair: T2.2a, IPC-UL actuation (Cantelli cushion on
 the stock TPC target)

First closed-loop PktR actuation (UL, Tier-A, gNB-only). The stock PUSCH
closed-loop power control already drives measured SINR toward a fixed target via
TPC {-1,0,+1,+3} dB with a 40 ms prohibit + PHR cap; this makes that target
dynamic by adding the adaptive Cantelli reliability cushion sigma*k(beta) on top
of the operator's (MCS-sane) base target, so the beta-quantile of the SINR
distribution, not just its mean, clears the requirement.

- pktr_runtime_config.h: new `actuate` flag (KAIAIR_PKTR_ACTUATE, independent of
  the view's KAIAIR_PKTR_METRICS for clean A/B) + pktr_ul_sinr_offset_db(): the
  single home of the actuation policy. Returns the cushion sigma*k(beta), or 0
  when actuation is off, the link has no stats, or sigma is in the
  regime-transition zone, a transient/stale sigma spike must never over-drive UL
  power (the bistable-link safety finding from the 2 Mbps collapse run).
- pusch_power_controller::compute_tpc_command() takes a sinr-target offset (default
  0 = stock); ue_cell_grid_allocator computes it from the UE's pktr_link_state at
  the call site and passes it in.
- view: [config] line shows UL-actuate ON/off.
- pktr_runtime_config_test: 4 new gating cases (off, no-samples, steady-cushion,
  sigma-spike-suppressed).

Default-off, so behaviour is byte-for-byte stock unless KAIAIR_PKTR_ACTUATE=1.
First live A/B to run at 250 kbps (monostable, safe); 2 Mbps collapse is left for
the scheduling half. All KaiAir edits tagged with inline // KaiAir/PktR comments.

Verified on the ARA gNB container: pktr_{link_state,ipc,runtime_config}_test pass;
scheduler_test 100% (no regression); gnb links clean.
